@* HelpCommentsPage: help topic "Comments and threads" at "/help/comments-and-threads". Static text and screenshots. *@
@page "/help/comments-and-threads"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="comments-and-threads">
    <section class="card">
        <ul>
            <li>Click the <strong>+</strong> at a line to start a thread about that line. Hold Shift and click another
                line on the same side to comment on a range. To comment on the whole file instead, leave the line
                fields empty.</li>
            <li>A thread is either a <strong>Question</strong> (the default) or a <strong>Finding</strong>. A
                Question is chat: ask, answer, and move on. A Finding goes in the report: it is part of what the
                reviewers sign. Choose the kind when you start the thread. Change your mind later with
                <strong>Make this a Finding</strong> or <strong>Make this a Question</strong>.</li>
            <li>A reply is chat unless you tick <strong>Add to report</strong>; a reply that is in the report is marked
                <strong>In report</strong>. The author of a reply or the lead of the review can add it to the report or
                take it out again later.</li>
            <li>Anyone signed in who may take part can <strong>reply</strong> and reopen a resolved thread. To
                <strong>resolve</strong> a Finding write a short resolution note, for example <em>fixed in abc123</em>,
                <em>ticket #123</em> or <em>not an issue</em>; for a Question the note is optional. The report prints a
                Finding together with its resolution note.</li>
            <li>Make a Question a Finding: the person who started the thread, any reviewer of the review, or the lead.
                Make a Finding a Question: only the person who started the thread or the lead. Auditors and a
                concluded review can change nothing.</li>
            <li>Posted comments cannot be edited or deleted. Chat never makes a signature out of date, but anything
                that changes the report does (a Finding, a reply added to the report, a resolution note); the page
                tells you which signatures it affects before you confirm. An open thread of either kind blocks signing
                until it is resolved.</li>
            <li>The <strong>Link</strong> on a thread is a stable address of that thread. Press
                <strong>Copy link</strong> to copy it and paste it into a ticket; whoever opens it signs in if
                needed and lands on the same place.</li>
        </ul>
        <figure class="help-figure">
            <img class="help-shot" src="/help/comments-and-threads-1.png" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A comment thread under a line of the diff, showing the comment, the thread state, the Link and Copy link buttons, and the Reply and Resolve buttons." />
            <figcaption>A thread under the line it is about.</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
